<title>FRANCE: BNP gains further in UAP/AXA terms.</title>
<headline>BNP gains further in UAP/AXA terms.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in bank Banque Nationale de Paris (BNP), owner of a large stake in Union des Assurances de Paris (UAP), rose further after merger terms with AXA were announced.</p>
<p>At 1146 GMT, BNP was up 4.85 percent at 209.90 francs. The share had opened 3.05 percent higher on the first alliance details but the share swap conditions were not known then.</p>
<p>At the end of 1995, BNP held a 17.3 percent stake in UAP.</p>
</text>
